# XCU set
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/set.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.set.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/remaining arguments shall be assigned
class      required
says       set with operands replaces all positional parameters and $# with
           them; earlier ones that are not replaced become unset.
test       t/001-positional.sh

assertion  XCU.set.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/without <i>argument</i> shall
class      required
says       set -- with no operands unsets all positional parameters; after
           --, operands that begin with - or + are plain parameters and set
           no options.
test       t/002-double-hyphen.sh

assertion  XCU.set.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/names and values of all
class      required
says       set with no options or operands lists the shell variables as
           name=value in the collation order of the current locale, with
           values quoted so that the lines can be read back.
test       t/003-listing.sh

assertion  XCU.set.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Write the current settings
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Write the current option settings
class      required
says       set -o writes the option settings to standard output and set +o
           writes commands that read back into the same option settings.
test       t/004-options-list.sh

assertion  XCU.set.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Set the <i>export</i> attribute for all variable assignments
class      required
since      2024
says       With set -a, every variable assignment (plain, by an expansion,
           by read) gives the variable the export attribute; set +a ends
           that.
test       t/005-allexport.sh

assertion  XCU.set.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Prevent existing regular files
class      required
says       With set -C, > does not overwrite an existing regular file (the
           command fails) but >| does, and a file that does not exist yet or
           a non-regular file such as /dev/null can still be the target of
           >.
test       t/006-noclobber.sh

assertion  XCU.set.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/immediately shall exit
class      required
says       With set -e, a failing command ends the shell at once with the
           failed command's status.
test       t/007-errexit.sh

assertion  XCU.set.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall be ignored when executing the compound list
class      required
says       set -e does not end the shell for a failure in an if, elif, while
           or until condition, in a command preceded by !, or in a command
           of an AND-OR list other than the last.
test       t/008-errexit-ignored.sh

assertion  XCU.set.009
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/multi-command pipeline
class      required
says       Under set -e, a failing command that is not the last of a
           pipeline, a failing subshell inside a pipeline whose last command
           succeeds, and a failing subshell for a command substitution do
           not end the shell; a failing pipeline does.
test       t/009-errexit-pipeline.sh

assertion  XCU.set.010
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/If the exit status of a compound command
class      required
says       Under set -e, a compound command (other than a subshell) whose
           non-zero status came from a failure while -e was ignored does not
           end the shell.
test       t/010-errexit-compound.sh

assertion  XCU.set.011
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/disable pathname expansion
class      required
says       With set -f pathname expansion is off, with set +f it is on
           again.
test       t/011-noglob.sh

assertion  XCU.set.012
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/read commands but does not execute them
class      required
says       With set -n the shell reads but does not execute the commands
           that follow, and exits with status zero.
test       t/012-noexec.sh

assertion  XCU.set.013
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/an unset parameter other than
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       With set -u, expanding an unset parameter other than @ and *
           writes a message to standard error and the non-interactive shell
           exits with a non-zero status; $@ and $* are exempt.
test       t/013-nounset.sh

assertion  XCU.set.014
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/write its input to standard error as it is read
class      required
says       With set -v the shell writes the input it reads to standard
           error.
test       t/014-verbose.sh

assertion  XCU.set.015
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/trace for each command after it expands
class      required
says       With set -x the shell writes a trace of each command to standard
           error after expanding it.
test       t/015-xtrace.sh

assertion  XCU.set.016
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Equivalent to
class      required
says       The long forms set -o allexport, noglob and noclobber act like
           -a, -f and -C, and set +o name turns them off again.
test       t/016-long-names.sh

assertion  XCU.set.017
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Equivalent to
class      required
says       The long forms set -o errexit, nounset, noexec, verbose and
           xtrace act like -e, -u, -n, -v and -x.
test       t/017-long-names-2.sh

assertion  XCU.set.018
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Derive the exit status of a pipeline
class      required
since      2024
says       set -o pipefail makes a pipeline fail when any command in it
           fails, using the rightmost failing status; set +o pipefail
           restores the default.
test       t/018-pipefail.sh

assertion  XCU.set.019
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/invalid option was specified
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       An invalid option given to set is an error: the status is non-
           zero, a non-interactive shell may exit (the error is a special
           built-in error).
test       t/019-invalid-option.sh

assertion  XCU.set.020
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall be supported if the implementation supports the User Portability
class      conditional
when       UP
says       The options -b, -m, ignoreeof, monitor, notify and nolog are
           accepted in both forms.
test       t/020-up-options.sh
